hadiths[45]{hadithnumber,text}:
"325","´﻿ Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) went to Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was in Iraq, and one day the prayer was delayed. He said, “O Mughira! What have you done? Do you not know that (one day) Jibreel (peace be upon him) came and he led the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also prayed (at that time). Then (Jibreel) led the second prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also prayed. Then (Jibreel) led the third prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also prayed. Then (Jibreel) led the fourth prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also prayed. Then (Jibreel) led the fifth prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also prayed. Then Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ‘I have been commanded to do so.’”"
"326","`Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` they were sitting with the Commander of the Faithful, ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), when he said, “Who among you remembers the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the trial (fitnah)?” I said, “I remember it exactly as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said it.” The Commander of the Faithful, ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), said, “Then relate it.” So I said, “The trial that befalls a man concerning his wife, his wealth, and his children is expiated by prayer, fasting, charity, enjoining good, and forbidding evil.” The Commander of the Faithful, ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), said, “I do not mean this, but rather the trial which will surge like the waves of the sea.” Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Commander of the Faithful! You have nothing to fear from that trial, for there is a closed door between you and it.” The Commander of the Faithful, ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), said, “Will the door be broken or opened?” Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “It will be broken.” Then the Commander of the Faithful, ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), said, “Then it will never be closed again.” Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked, “Did ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) know what the door was?” He said, “Yes, just as you know that night follows day.” (Sayyiduna Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him) narrated a hadith that was not mistaken. So he was asked about the door, and he said, “The door was the Commander of the Faithful, Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him).”"
"327","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): A man kissed a (non-mahram) woman, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him about it. So Allah, the Most Great and Exalted, revealed this verse: ""Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in some hours of the night. Indeed, good deeds erase bad deeds."" The man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Is this only for me?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""It is for my entire Ummah."""
"328","In another narration, it is reported from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): ""For every one among my Ummah who commits (minor sins), this (is an expiation) for him."""
"329","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""Which deed is most beloved to Allah?"" He replied, ""Prayer, which is performed at its proper time."" I then asked, ""After that, which one?"" He (peace be upon him) said, ""After that, obedience to parents."" I asked again, ""After that, which one?"" He (peace be upon him) said, ""Striving in the way of Allah."" Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned to me only this much, and if I had asked him for more, he would have told me more."
"330","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""If there was a river at the door of any one of you in which he bathed five times a day, do you think that any dirt would remain on him?"" The Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, replied: ""Nothing of his dirt would remain."" So the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""This is the example of the five prayers; Allah wipes out sins through them."""
"331","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be moderate in prostrations, and none of you should spread his hands like a dog. And when spitting, he should not spit in front of himself nor to his right side, because he is conversing with his Lord."""
"332","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When the heat becomes intense, perform the prayer when it cools down, because the severity of heat is from the raging of Hell. And Hell complained to its Lord and said: O my Lord! One part of me has consumed another part. So Allah allowed it two breaths, one in the winter and one in the summer. And that is the severe heat which you feel and the severe cold which you experience."""
"333","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The mu’adhdhin wanted to give the adhan for Zuhr, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: “Let it cool down.” Then he wanted to give the adhan again, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: “Let it cool down.” This continued until we saw the shade of the hills. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “The severity of heat is from the boiling of Hell, so when the heat is intense, perform (the Zuhr) prayer when it cools down.”"
"334","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that (one day) when the sun had declined, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out and performed the Zuhr prayer. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood on the pulpit and mentioned the Day of Resurrection and stated: ""There will be great events in it."" After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wants to ask something, let him ask. Whatever you ask me, I will tell you as long as I am in this place."" So the people wept a lot, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said several times: ""Ask me."" Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hudhafah Sahmi (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and asked, ""Who is my father?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your father is Hudhafah."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) kept saying: ""Ask me."" So the Commander of the Faithful, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), sat down on his knees and said: ""We are pleased with Allah, Glorious is His Majesty, as our Lord, with Islam as our religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) as our Prophet."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became silent. After that, he said that Paradise and Hell have just been presented before me in this corner of the wall; I have never seen anything as excellent (as Paradise) and anything as terrible (as Hell)."""
"335","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer the Fajr prayer at such a time that each of us could recognize the person sitting next to him. In it, he would recite between sixty and one hundred verses. He used to offer the Zuhr prayer when the sun had just declined (from its zenith), and the Asr prayer at such a time that one of us could go to the outskirts of Madinah and return, but the sun would still be shining brightly. The narrator (Abu Minhal) says: And regarding Maghrib, I forgot what was said. And as for delaying the Isha prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not mind delaying it up to one-third of the night. After that, the narrator said: up to half the night."
"336","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered eight rak‘ahs of Zuhr and Asr and seven rak‘ahs of Maghrib and Isha (together) in Madinah."
"337","The hadith regarding the times of prayer from Sayyiduna Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) has been mentioned earlier (see the previous hadith, in which the time of Asr is stated), and in this narration, while mentioning Isha, (Abu Barzah, may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""And they used to dislike sleeping before the Isha prayer and talking after it."" (And then the entire hadith is narrated.)"
"338","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): We would have finished offering the Asr prayer, and then someone would go to the tribe of Banu Amr bin Auf and find them offering the Asr prayer."
"339","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Asr prayer at a time when the sun was high and bright. Then a person would go to Awali (the outskirts of Madinah) and reach those people at a time when the sun was still high, and some places in Awali are four miles or close to that from Madinah."
"340","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The person who misses the Asr prayer is as if his family and wealth have been destroyed."""
"341","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) that on a rainy day during a battle, he said: ""Pray the Asr prayer early, because the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever misses the Asr prayer, surely his (good) deeds are lost.'"""
"342","Sayedna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we were with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) when he looked at the moon and said: ""Indeed, you will see your Lord just as you are seeing this moon. You will not feel any difficulty or trouble in seeing Him."" Therefore, if you can avoid being overpowered (by Satan) regarding the prayers before sunrise and before sunset, then do so. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) recited this verse: ""So glorify your Lord with His praise before the rising of the sun and before its setting."""
"343","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Some angels come to you in succession during the night and some during the day, and they all gather at the Fajr and Asr prayers. Then those angels who have stayed with you during the night ascend (to the heavens), and their Lord asks them, although He knows best about His servants, 'In what condition did you leave My servants?' They say, 'We left them while they were praying, and when we arrived to them (then also) they were praying.'"""
"344","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you gets one rak'ah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets, he should complete his prayer, and when he gets one rak'ah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, he should (also) complete his prayer."""
"345","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) used to say: ""The duration of your existence, in comparison to the nations that passed before you, is like the time between the Asr prayer and sunset. The people of the Torah were given the Torah and they worked until half the day had passed; they became tired and were each given one qirat. Then the people of the Gospel were given the Gospel and they worked until the Asr prayer; then they became tired and were each given one qirat. After that, we were given the Qur'an and we worked until sunset, so we were given two qirats each. Both the people of the Book said, 'O our Lord! You gave these people two qirats and gave us only one qirat, even though we did more work.' Allah the Exalted said, 'Did I withhold anything from your wages?' They replied, 'No.' So Allah the Almighty said, 'This is My mercy; I give it to whom I will (what objection do you have?).'"""
"346","Sayyiduna Rafi' bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we used to offer the Maghrib prayer with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then each of us would return (after the prayer) at such a time that he could see the places where his arrows had fallen."
"347","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer the Zuhr prayer exactly at midday, and the Asr prayer at a time when the sun was still bright and shining, and the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set, and the Isha prayer sometimes at one time, sometimes at another. When he (peace be upon him) saw that the people had gathered, he would offer it early, and when he saw that the people were late, he would delay it. And the Fajr prayer, those people—or he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)—used to offer in darkness."
"348","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that’ the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Let not the Bedouins overpower you regarding the name of your Maghrib prayer (i.e., let them not give it another name).” And he said: “The Bedouins say that it (i.e., Maghrib) is ‘Isha.”"
"349","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that one night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed the 'Isha prayer, and this incident was before the spread of Islam. So, he (peace be upon him) did not come out until Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to him and said, ""The women and children have fallen asleep."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came out and said, ""Among the people of the earth, none are waiting for this prayer except you."""
"350","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I and my companions who had come with me by boat were staying at Baqi’ Bathan, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in Madinah. So, one group after another from among us would go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in turns. Then (one day) all of us, that is, I and my companions, went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was busy with his work, so he delayed the (‘Isha) prayer until half the night had passed. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and led the people in prayer. Then, when he had finished his prayer, he said to those who were present: “At this time, no one is praying except you,” or he said something like: “No one has prayed.” I do not know which of these two sentences he said. Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We returned, happy with what we had heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"351","The hadith of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the ‘Isha prayer, so Amir al-Mu’minin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) called out to him. This has been mentioned earlier (see the Book: Statement of the Times of Prayer... Chapter: The Virtue of the ‘Isha Prayer...). In this narration, she adds that the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) used to offer the (‘Isha) prayer after the disappearance of the twilight until the first third of the night. And in the narration of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): “The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, as if I am looking at him at that moment, water was dripping from his blessed head and he had his hand placed on his blessed head, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ‘If I did not consider it hard upon my Ummah, I would have certainly commanded them to offer the ‘Isha prayer in this manner (at this time).’”"
"352","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his hand on his head, he separated his fingers a little and placed the tips of his fingers on one side of his head. Then, joining them together, he drew them across his head in such a way that his thumb reached his earlobe, near the edge of his beard by his face. He neither delayed nor hurried; he did exactly as I have described to you."
"353","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him)` (regarding the ‘Isha prayer) narrates that it is as if I am seeing the shine of the ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that night."
"354","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs the two cool prayers will enter Paradise."""
"355","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) told me that the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) ate suhoor with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and then stood up for prayer. So I asked, ""How much time was there between the two?"" Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""The time it takes to recite fifty or sixty verses (of the Qur'an)."""
"356","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I used to eat sahur with my family, then I would hurry so that I could perform the Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"357","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Some beloved personalities mentioned before me, and the most beloved among them to me was the Commander of the Faithful, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), stated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade performing prayer after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and after the Asr prayer until the sun sets."
"358","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(O people!) Do not perform your prayers at the time of sunrise nor at the time of sunset."""
"359","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the edge of the sun appears, stop praying until the sun rises high, and when the edge of the sun sets, stop praying until (the whole sun) has set."""
"360","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two types of sales and two types of clothing (and this hadith has already been mentioned, see the Book: Description of Prayer... Chapter: Covering that which must be covered). In this hadith, it is further stated: ""And he forbade two prayers: (1) He forbade prayer after Fajr until the sun rises properly, and (2) after Asr until the sun sets properly."""
"361","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Amir Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him): He said, (O people!) You perform a prayer such that indeed we kept the company of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), but we never saw him perform it, and certainly he forbade it—meaning the two rak‘ahs after ‘Asr."
"362","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: By the One who took the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) from this world, the Prophet (peace be upon him) never abandoned the two rak’ahs after Asr until he met Allah, and when he (peace be upon him) met Allah, at that time (due to the heaviness of the body) he (peace be upon him) would become burdened from prayer, and he (peace be upon him) would perform many of his prayers sitting, and the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) would always perform these two rak’ahs, that is, the two rak’ahs after Asr, and he would perform them at home, out of fear that it might become burdensome for his Ummah. The Prophet (peace be upon him) liked only that which would be easy for his Ummah."
"363","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) never abandoned two units of prayer, whether in secret or in public: two units before the Fajr prayer and two units after the Asr prayer."
"364","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We traveled one night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so some people said, ""If only you (peace be upon him) would rest with all of us at the end of the night."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""I fear that you may sleep and become heedless of the (Fajr) prayer."" So Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I will wake you all up."" Therefore, everyone lay down and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) sat leaning his back against his camel, but sleep also overcame him and he too fell asleep. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up at such a time that the edge of the sun had risen. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""O Bilal! What happened to what you said?"" He replied, ""Such sleep has never been cast over me before."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""(It is true) Allah took your souls whenever He wished and returned them whenever He wished. O Bilal! Get up and give the call to prayer for the people."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ablution, and when the sun had risen high and become white, the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up and offered the prayer."
"365","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that Amir al-Mu'minin Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to his place after sunset during the (battle of) Khandaq and began to speak ill of the disbelievers of Quraysh. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I could not perform the Asr prayer until the sun had set."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""By Allah, I too have not performed the Asr prayer (until now)."" Then we turned towards (the place) Bathan, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution for the prayer, and all of us also performed ablution for the prayer. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the Asr prayer after the sun had set, and after that he performed the Maghrib prayer."
"366","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever forgets any prayer, he should offer it when he remembers it; its expiation is only this. Because Allah Almighty (in Surah 'Taha') says: 'And establish prayer for My remembrance.'"""
"367","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Behold! The people have offered the prayer and gone to sleep, while you are considered to be in prayer as long as you are waiting for the prayer."""
"368","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) once offered the Isha prayer in the last part of his life... till the end (has passed, see the Book: Statement of Knowledge... Chapter: Talking about knowledge at night...). And in this hadith, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, after one hundred years, none of those who are on the earth today will remain."" By this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) meant that this generation (era) will pass away."
"369","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Ashab al-Suffah were some poor people, and the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said: ""Whoever has food for two people should take a third (from among them), and if he has food for four, then let him take a fifth or a sixth from among them."" And the Commander of the Faithful, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), took three people, and the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took ten. Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was there, and my parents. (The narrator of the hadith, Abu Uthman, said:) And I do not know whether he also said (or not) that my wife and our servant, who was shared between me and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), were also there. And Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) had dinner at the house of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stayed there for a while where the Isha prayer was offered. After returning, he stayed for a while until the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rested, then after that, as much of the night as Allah willed, he spent there (and then) came to his house. His wife said to him: Who kept you away from your guests? Or she said: From your guest? He replied: Did you not feed them? She said: They did not agree to eat until you came. The food was presented before them, but they refused. Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I, out of fear, went and hid. Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O you mean one!"" and then scolded very harshly, and said to the guests: ""Eat to your fill."" After that, he said: ""By Allah! I will never eat."" Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) says: By Allah, whenever we took a morsel, it increased beneath it. Then, when all the guests were satisfied and more food was left than before, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) looked at it, and it was as much as before or even more. So he said to his wife: ""O sister of Bani Firas! What is this matter?"" She replied: ""By the coolness of my eyes! Surely, it is now three times more than before."" Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) ate from it and said: ""This, that is, my oath, was from Satan."" In the end, he took a morsel from it. After that, he took it to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in the morning it was still there. There was a treaty between us and a people, and its term had expired, so we separated twelve men. With each of them were some people—by Allah, I do not know how many people were with each person. All of them ate from that food, or he said something similar."
